.TH PVE\-EXT\-PATCH 8 "2026-09-17" "pve-ext" "Proxmox VE"
.SH NAME
pve\-ext\-patch \- apply, verify, remove and report pve\-ext managed patches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pve\-ext\-patch
.RI [ \-\-root
.IR dir ]
.RI { apply | remove | verify | status }
.RI [ manifest ...]
.br
.B pve\-ext\-patch
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pve\-ext\-patch
dpkg\-diverts a stock Proxmox VE file away, regenerates the real path as
pristine original plus a manifest's unified diff in a scratch copy, gates
installation on a syntax/template check, and only then installs the
result. Manifests are TOML files under
.IR /usr/share/pve\-ext/patches/ *.toml .
See
.I pve\-ext/README.md
in the pve\-meta source tree for the manifest format and worked examples.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI apply\ [manifest...]
Diverts each entry's file (if not already), applies its diff with
.B "patch \-p1 \-\-fuzz=0" ,
gates on a clean \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR then the entry's
.B check
(perl\ \-c, or a template marker/\fB</body>\fR check), then
.BR install (1)s
the result. Best\-effort per file. Refuses to touch a file diverted by a
different package. Must run as root, unless
.B \-\-root
is given.
.TP
.BI remove\ [manifest...]
Restores each entry's pristine file and removes its diversion. Must run as
root, unless
.B \-\-root
is given.
.TP
.BI verify\ [manifest...]
Dry\-runs
.RI ( "patch \-\-dry\-run" )
each entry's diff against its pristine copy and reports hunks\-would\-apply
versus hunks\-failed. Makes no changes; safe to run unprivileged and
against
.BR \-\-root .
.TP
.BI status\ [manifest...]
Reports, per file: diversion state and owner, pristine backup presence,
whether the marker is present, and whether the live file is byte\-for\-byte
in sync with pristine\ +\ diff.
.PP
With no
.I manifest
arguments, every command acts on every
.I *.toml
file under the manifest directory. A
.I manifest
argument is either a bare name (resolved to
.IR name .toml
under that directory) or a path to a manifest file directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-root\ dir
Resolve every path this tool touches \(em including dpkg\-divert
diversions, scratch backups and the failure log \(em under
.I dir
instead of
.IR / ,
and pass it through to
.BR dpkg\-divert (1).
Intended for CI/dev use against an extracted package tree.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success. Non\-zero if any selected file failed to apply/remove/verify,
if no manifest or no
.B [[file]]
entries were found, or for a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/pve\-ext/patches/*.toml
Installed manifests; in a checkout, falls back to
.I ../patches
next to this script.
.TP
.I <path>.pve\-ext\-orig
The pristine backup dpkg\-divert creates for a diverted
.IR path .
.TP
.I <root>/run/pve\-ext\-patch/failed
Append\-only failure log (never only stderr, which a postinst commonly
swallows).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dpkg\-divert (1),
.BR patch (1);
.I pve\-ext/README.md
in the pve\-meta source tree.
.SH AUTHOR
Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>
